WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:04.675
Lab 1 runs in the kit's folder
against fictional fixtures.

3
00:00:04.675 --> 00:00:09.175
Step one runs the drift and
comparison tests: seventeen pass.

4
00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.900
Step two runs day one.

5
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:15.192
The summary counts four attribute
drifts, two missing identities,

6
00:00:15.192 --> 00:00:19.563
three orphan accounts, two stale
access and one unauthorized write,

7
00:00:19.563 --> 00:00:23.075
and lists credential and
schema drift as not computed.

8
00:00:23.075 --> 00:00:26.375
Then a one-line script prints
Erin's and Carol's rows.

9
00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:30.692
Erin's department: HR expects
HR, but Entra ID holds Finance,

10
00:00:30.692 --> 00:00:34.200
and the audit shows a
help-desk account wrote it.

11
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.687
That's both attribute drift
and an unauthorized write.

12
00:00:37.687 --> 00:00:41.738
Her manager differs too, in
Entra ID and in SailPoint.

13
00:00:41.738 --> 00:00:45.700
Carol is terminated in HR,
but enabled in Entra ID

14
00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:49.820
and not disabled in SailPoint:
stale access, twice.
